  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M.Kaja Mohindeen vs State Rep By on 9 February, 2022 Author: A.D.Jagadish Chandira Bench: A.D.Jagadish Chandira Crl.O.P.No In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 09.02.2022 Coram : The Honourable Mr.Justice A.D.Jagadish Chandira Crl.O.P.No.2761 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.Nos.1282 & 1283 of 2022 M.Kaja Mohindeen ..",
    "facts": "This Criminal Original Petition has been filed by the petitioner/A3 to quash the complaint in CC.No.131 of 2017 pending on the file of the Judicial Magistrate, Ambattur, Chennai. 2. It is the case of the complainant that one Manna Health Mix, Southern Health Foods Pvt Ltd., is the manufacturer of the alleged health drinks and samples were lifted and the same were sent for the analysis and report was received on 10.06.2014. As per the report, the sample were found to be sub-standard, unsafe and misbranded. Thereby, the respondent/complainant had filed the private complaint against the petitioner and other accused for the offence under Sections 3(1)(zx), 3(1)(zz)(v)(x) and 3(1)(zf)(a-i) of Food Safety and Standardization Act, 2006. The subsequent samples also reveal that the product was sub-standard and unsafe.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that admittedly, as per the complaint, the health mix which was subjected to test was produced by Southern Health Food Private Limited having office at AL-84, 1st Floor, 4th Street, II Main Road, Anna Nagar, Chennai - 40 and the petitioner is the nominee of the company and as per the Section 66 of FSS Act, a mandate is cast on the complainant to proceed against the company which has produced whereas in this case, the company was not impleded. The private complaint which has been filed without impleding the company is bad in law, thereby he prayed for quashing the proceedings. Further, the learned counsel would submit that in respect of a co-accused in the very same case, this Court in Crl.OP.No.19747 of 2017 dated 26.11.2021 taking into consideration that the company was not impleaded as accused, has [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings. 5. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor submitted that as per the Section 66 of the Act, when the offences are committed by the company, the company has to be added as an accused. However, he would fairly concede that the company has not been added as accused in this case. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 6. Perusal of records including the complaint reveals that the health mix had been produced by M/s.Southern Health Food Private Limited.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that admittedly, as per the complaint, the health mix which was subjected to test was produced by Southern Health Food Private Limited having office at AL-84, 1st Floor, 4th Street, II Main Road, Anna Nagar, Chennai - 40 and the petitioner is the nominee of the company and as per the Section 66 of FSS Act, a mandate is cast on the complainant to proceed against the company which has produced whereas in this case, the company was not impleded. The private complaint which has been filed without impleding the company is bad in law, thereby he prayed for quashing the proceedings. Further, the learned counsel would submit that in respect of a co-accused in the very same case, this Court in Crl.OP.No.19747 of 2017 dated 26.11.2021 taking into consideration that the company was not impleaded as accused, has [LEAKAGE_MASK] the proceedings. 5. The learned Additional Public Prosecutor submitted that as per the Section 66 of the Act, when the offences are committed by the company, the company has to be added as an accused. However, he would fairly concede that the company has not been added as accused in this case. https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 6. Perusal of records including the complaint reveals that the health mix had been produced by M/s.Southern Health Food Private Limited.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
